subtitle: Cheap and inclusive, but the public sees no common preparation.
on-arrival: budget_2019_preparation = "Separate current and movement briefs"; party_unity -= 2; barons_dissent -= 2; spring_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent -= 2; union_trust += 1; progressives_dissent -= 2; razem_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Party currents and labour organisers file separate budget briefs"

Each party current puts its red line on paper; Lewica Pracy MPs and union
organisers file workplace demands alongside them. The February conference must
still turn those briefs into two priorities and one recorded tactic.

- @lgbt_zones_2019: Turn to the county resolutions

@lgbt_zones_2019
# prose-audit: Grade C — The county resolutions, the atlas and the European vote are staged with three distinct Lewica lines; the residents of the declared counties are described rather than heard.
title: The counties that declare themselves free
subtitle: A third of the country is covered by anti-LGBT resolutions and Europe has noticed
face-image: img/poland/events/lgbt-free-zones-2020.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.lgbt_zones_2019_done = 1;
Q.minority_safety = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 50) - 8
);
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 10;
Q.far_right_agenda = (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) + 3;
Q.zone_resolution_count = 90;
Q.news_headline =
    "Around a third of Poland is covered by anti-LGBT county resolutions";
!}

= December 2019 — Ninety resolutions and a map

Since the summer, county and municipal councils have been adopting resolutions
declaring themselves free of what the texts call LGBT ideology. Roughly ninety
of them now exist, covering something close to a third of the country by area.
They have no legal force. They also have addresses: a young person in one of
those counties knows their own council has voted on whether they are an
ideology.

In Białystok in July, the city's first equality march was met by organised
groups who threw stones and bottles at marchers while police lines held and
sometimes did not. Two activists have published an online atlas of the
resolutions, and are being sued for it. The European Parliament has just
condemned the declarations by a large majority, which the government uses as
proof that the whole thing was invented in Brussels.

We have forty-nine deputies and no county councils to speak of. What we have is
a choice about whether this is a national argument, a legal one, or a local
organising problem.

[? if independence_march_strategy = "Counter-mobilisation": Our people were
already in the street against the nationalist organisers in November, which
means the networks exist and are tired.?]
[? if independence_march_strategy = "Join the Independence March": Having
marched in the November procession, our credibility with the people targeted by
these resolutions is the first thing that will be questioned.?]
[? if presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń": Our presidential candidate is
the most prominent openly gay politician in the country, which makes this
unavoidable and makes every response read as self-interest.?]

- @zones_legal
- @zones_local
- @zones_national
- @zones_europe

@zones_legal
title: Fund the legal challenges and defend the atlas authors
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Slow, technical, and the only route that eventually deletes resolutions.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no legal fund and no capacity to build one this month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.zones_response = "Legal challenge";
Q.zone_legal_campaign = 1;
Q.minority_safety = (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 42) + 6;
Q.judicial_repair_mandate =
    (Number(Q.judicial_repair_mandate) || 0) + 3;
Q.movement_autonomy = (Number(Q.movement_autonomy) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 10;
Q.far_right_agenda = (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) - 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left funds administrative-court challenges to the county resolutions";
!}

Administrative courts, one resolution at a time, plus lawyers for the two
people being sued for publishing a map of public documents. It is unglamorous
and it works: a resolution struck down by a court is gone in a way that a
resolution argued with on television is not.

The first judgments take a year. By then the file has a shape — which councils,
which wording, which legal defect — and that file is what makes the money
argument possible when Brussels starts attaching conditions to cohesion funds.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@zones_local
title: Build the answer inside the declared counties themselves
subtitle: Puts organisers where the resolutions passed instead of where the sympathetic voters are; the slowest route and the only one that changes a council.
on-arrival: {!
Q.zones_response = "Local organising";
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 5;
Q.minority_safety = (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 42) + 3;
Q.organiser_energy = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.organiser_energy) || 50) - 4
);
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) + 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 5;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.progressives_dissent =
    (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) + 3;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica organisers move into the counties that passed the resolutions";
!}

We stop treating the declared counties as enemy territory and start treating
them as places where people we are supposed to represent are living. Small
rooms, library meetings, one councillor at a time, no cameras.

Our metropolitan organisers hate it and say the party is being asked to be
polite to bigots. What it produces, over years rather than months, is councils
in which somebody will move the repeal — which nobody in Warsaw can do from a
studio.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@zones_national
title: Make the resolutions a national argument about who the state is for
subtitle: The loudest and fastest response; it raises the salience of a fight the right is currently winning.
on-arrival: {!
Q.zones_response = "National confrontation";
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 10;
Q.progressive_credibility =
    (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) + 5;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 3;
Q.minority_safety = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 42) - 3
);
Q.far_right_agenda = (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) + 4;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) - 3;
Q.cultural_issue_salience =
    (Number(Q.cultural_issue_salience) || 0) + 6;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left makes the county resolutions a national argument";
!}

Every studio, every week: read the wording out, ask the councillor who signed
it to explain it to a fifteen-year-old in their own town, refuse to accept the
word *ideology* as a description of a person.

It is the correct argument and it makes the subject bigger. The government
wanted a culture war going into a presidential year and we have agreed to have
one on its chosen ground, where its side starts with the larger crowd and the
public broadcaster.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@zones_europe
title: Take the map to Brussels and ask for money to be conditioned on it
subtitle: Effective and it hands the government its favourite sentence about foreign interference.
on-arrival: {!
Q.zones_response = "European conditionality";
Q.zone_eu_conditionality = 1;
Q.eu_relations = (Number(Q.eu_relations) || 50) + 5;
Q.minority_safety = (Number(Q.minority_safety) || 42) + 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 8;
Q.far_right_agenda = (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 0) + 3;
Q.rural_support = (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) - 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) - 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The county resolutions are put in front of the European Commission";
!}

Our MEPs and deputies take the atlas to the Commission with a single request:
before a partnership programme sends money to a council, ask whether that
council has voted on the existence of its own residents.

It is the most effective instrument available and it costs exactly what
everyone predicts. For the next three years, every conversation about these
resolutions in a rural hall begins with a Polish party having asked Brussels to
withhold money from a Polish county.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue
